    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`). The suite's sole test class is `AcceptanceTest`, and its new `coreFlagsPossibleDuplicate` case is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the soft-duplicate flag for `POST /api/owners` following the OfficeFloor function-injection pattern, keeping structural impact low.\n\n**New behaviour** lives in one small, cohesive function class (`WMC_other` \u2248 0) rather than growing any existing class:\n\n- **`FlagPossibleDuplicate.java`** (new) \u2014 a single-method step that scans existing owners for one sharing the new owner's normalized `lastName` + `postcode` with a *different* telephone. On a match it sets `possibleDuplicate=true` and `possibleDuplicateOf=<matching id>`; otherwise `possibleDuplicate=false`. It runs after the hard-duplicate guards (`RequireUniqueIdentity`) so only non-blocking soft matches reach it. It mutates the `@Val Owner` in place before `save`, so the values persist and reappear on later `GET`s.\n\n**Supporting edits** (each minimal, no method bodies grown):\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted a `flagDuplicate` step between `countHousehold` and `save`, under the same `transaction` governance.\n- `Owner.java` \u2014 two persisted fields (`possible_duplicate`, `possible_duplicate_of`) with plain accessors.\n- `db/hsqldb/schema.sql` \u2014 two matching columns (hsqldb is the test profile).\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 two read-only `Owner` DTO properties; MapStruct maps them by name, so no mapper change was needed.\n\nThe flow reuses the codebase's existing conventions (persisted derived fields like `namesakeCount`/`householdCount`, `@Val`-mutated entity, name-based MapStruct mapping), so the diff is small and localized.",
